==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|týna}}, from the root of {{m|is|tjón|t=loss, damage}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈtʰiːna/}}
** {{rhymes|is|iːna|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|týndi|týnt}}

# to [[lose]] (objects)

====Usage notes====
* The [[imperative]] mood of the verb '''''týna''''' (''[[týndu]]'') is most often used with a negative (the word {{m|is|ekki}}).
* It's not possible to "lose" insubstantial things like ''[[von]]'' ("[[hope]]") ''[[gleði]]'' ("[[joy]]"). For that the word ''[[missa]]'' would rather be used. (the exception to this is the phrase ''[[týna lífi|'''týna''' lífi]]'' meaning literally "to lose [one's] life" that is "to [[die]]").

